      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MiniMax H3 Ref2VA Grounding Guard — drop-in module\n\n**Copy the three colored groups into your existing MiniMax H3 Ref2VA workflow.**\n\n1. Replace the brief and both images. Keep the image order identical everywhere: `<Picture 1>` is the identity reference and `<Picture 2>` is the environment/style reference. If you use only one image, remove Picture 2 from both the batch and manifest.\n2. Connect the output of **8. CONNECT THIS OUTPUT** to the native `MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo` **prompt** input. Do not connect the splitter prompt directly; that bypasses fail-closed protection.\n3. Feed the same original images—not the resized analysis batch—to the native H3 `ref_image_1`, `ref_image_2`, ... sockets in exactly the same order.\n4. Share **Duration seconds** with your existing H3 frame-count math. You may also connect the splitter's width/height outputs to the matching H3 inputs.\n5. For identity + control video, connect your existing `VIDEO` object to **reference_video**, add one `<Video 1>: [dg:action,motion,camera,temporal,composition] ...` manifest line, and keep sending the decoded frames/audio through your existing H3 Ref2VA inputs.\n\nStrict mode blocks transport mismatch, malformed evidence, refusal, uncertainty, or insufficient role coverage before the expensive H3 render. The status and report previews explain the decision. The batch is for DiffusionGemma inspection only; the original references still drive MiniMax."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "title": "How to plug this into MiniMax H3 Ref2VA"
    },
